  "paraphrase": "For all functions f, g, h from ℝ to ℝ, and for all real numbers a, b with 0 in (a, b), if f, g, h are differentiable on (a, b), and for all x in (a, b), the derivatives of f, g, h satisfy specific conditions involving f(x), g(x), h(x), and their initial values at 0 are given, then there exist real numbers c, d with 0 in (c, d), such that for all x in (c, d), f(x) equals the putnam_2009_a2_solution(x)."
